BEGIN_DESC
Near the Sun, 0.0833 AU (12.46 million km, 17.9 solar radii): the critical mark of the heavy suit.
Niza Krit (Pantsir, Suit_T30, rated to +430 C) is at its rated limit here: the suit's surroundings are +430 C (the
radiative balance in full sunlight, 196 kW/m2 = 144 Suns). Any closer and the environment is out of the suit's limits.
Kaira Rean (Karkas, Suit_T10, set Boron) is far past her suit's limits here: its surroundings are ~+447 C against a
rating of +121 C and a damage onset of +190 C - get her into the glider at once.
The Delta-glider GL-01 is a few tens of metres away, all three on a circular orbit round the Sun (103 km/s).
END_DESC

